    {
      "id": 145,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to use Loki",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 108,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Loki is for logs.** Use it to find the exact error message, file path, line, stdout/stderr, and trace_id.\n\nFor the latest run, first find the latest `run_id`, then filter logs by that `run_id`.\n\n_Panels are scoped to the `exposure-automation-lab-playwright-runner*` container(s) so results only show real automation JSON logs — a plain `{environment=\"local\"}` selector also matches Loki/Grafana's own query logs (which echo the search string) and pollutes results with empty rows._\n\n_This stack does not emit `test_failed_summary` or a per-test trace log; the Failure Summary panel uses the `test_failed` event, and trace correlation uses the run-level `automation_trace_started` event. Automation logs reach Loki only when Playwright runs **inside Docker** (via the runner container → Alloy); host-only runs do not appear here._"
      }
    },
