    {
      "id": 65,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read Tempo",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 130,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### How to read Tempo\n\n- One trace usually represents one automation run.\n- `automation.run` is the root span.\n- `automation.test` spans represent individual tests.\n- Red / error spans represent failed tests.\n- Click a Trace ID and inspect Span attributes.\n- Important attributes: `test.name`, `test.suite`, `test.status`, `test.duration_ms`, `test.retry`, `automation.run_id`, artifact paths.\n- Tempo shows where in the execution flow the failure happened."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 107,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "G \u2014 Investigation Workflow",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 138,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": 160,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Investigation Workflow",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 139,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 12
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Investigation Workflow\n\n**Metric** tells you *something* broke.  \n**Log** tells you *why* it broke.  \n**Trace** tells you *where* it broke in the execution flow.\n\n### Investigation flow\n1. **Start with Prometheus Overview:** check failed tests, failure ratio, duration, and suite breakdown.\n2. **Go to Loki:** filter by latest `run_id` and failure logs. Find error message, file path, test name, and trace_id.\n3. **Go to Tempo:** open the trace_id. Inspect `automation.run` and failed `automation.test` spans.\n4. **Go to code:** fix the test, locator, data setup, app bug, or environment problem.\n\n### Architecture\n\n**Metrics:**  \nPlaywright CTRF JSON \u2192 automation-results-exporter \u2192 Prometheus \u2192 Grafana\n\n**Logs:**  \nWinston / console / stdout \u2192 Docker logs \u2192 Alloy \u2192 Loki \u2192 Grafana\n\n**Traces:**  \nPlaywright custom reporter \u2192 OpenTelemetry spans \u2192 Tempo \u2192 Grafana"
      }
    }
  ]
